    "source_issues_appended": [
      {
        "claim": "The printed p. 142 consequence calls the glued all-integer satellite system a universal graded connecting functor. Printed p. 140 gives an initial universal property only on finite nonnegative right truncations, while degree reversal transports the left step-minus-one construction's terminal property to finite nonpositive truncations; the opposite halfwise variances do not produce global initial universality.",
        "control": "Preserve the printed phrase in diplomatic French. Keep the D000214 mapping unchanged while creating production/p142_fix2, a fresh bilingual reader and visual witness, a stable-ID semantic successor reusing tohoku:thm:2.2.2:dual and tohoku:occ:p142:o003, and the audited Stacks left-satellite lemma. Resolve only in a later mapping successor whose replacement decision explicitly asserts halfwise universality and denies global all-integer universality.",
        "evidence": "Official Part I SHA-256 5A8E5720BC2EF8905BF85F7919C65AC4A87A31CFC854BD77E6B5084C0D2DEBEF, printed pp. 140 and 142. For F=(-) tensor_Z Z/2 on Ab, the glued exact system has S^{-1}(A)=A[2] and S^{-2}=0. The graded connecting functor U concentrated in degree -1 receives both the zero map and the identity in degree -1 from S with the same zero degree-zero component, so initial uniqueness fails.",
        "evidence_labels": "homology-lemma-finite-effaceability-universality;homology-lemma-right-satellites-injective-effacements;homology-lemma-graded-connecting-functor-dualities",
